📚 <b>Модуль: Advanced object model</b>

<b>Abstract base classes</b>
Python's object model supports protocols, controlled attributes, descriptors and deliberate interface design.

<b>Ключевая идея.</b> An abstract base class documents a required interface and prevents incomplete direct instances.

<b>Пример решения:</b>
<pre>from abc import ABC, abstractmethod
class Shape(ABC):
    @abstractmethod
    def area(self):
        pass
class Square(Shape):
    def __init__(self, side):
        self.side = side
    def area(self):
        return self.side ** 2
print(Square(4).area())</pre>

